{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "At the Clothing Store", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Oh! My Aching Feet", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > City Shoppers > A Clothing Sale", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately exchange information about buying things in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Parts of the Body", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Here are important parts of the body and how to talk about problems.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can say <span class = \"italic\">I have a headache, a backache, an earache</span>. <br/>You can also say<span class = \"italic\"> my head hurts, my back hurts</span> or <span class = \"italic\"> my ear hurts</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For other parts of the body, you say \u201churt\u201d: <span class = \"italic\">my feet hurt.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Another word for hurt is ache. You can say<span class = \"italic\"> my feet ache</span> or <span class = \"italic\"> my feet are aching</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have a headache.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My toe hurts!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Does your nose hurt?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My left wrist aches.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Main parts of the body include ear, head, mouth, chin, nose, back, neck, elbow, wrist and foot.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hurt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel pain in a part of the body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My feet hurt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about parts of your body.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remove clothing or shoes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm taking off my shoes!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to relax", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to rest, to stop doing an activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It feels good to relax.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heavy", "type": "name"}, {"content": " weighing many kilograms or pounds", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These bags are heavy!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "part of the body you use to walk; plural form of foot", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My feet hurt! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "head", "type": "name"}, {"content": "part of the body with eyes, nose, mouth and ears ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My head is aching!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "blister", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sore mark on the skin, often caused by wearing new shoes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have blisters on my foot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pharmacy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a store where you can buy health products", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is there a pharmacy in this mall?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn2le07ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking and Saying Where Things Are", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can ask where something is with the question:  <span class=\"italic\"> \"Where is ... ?\"</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\"Is there a ... nearby?\"", "type": "describer"}, {"content": 